Radio SAWA - Libya رادیو سوا لیبیا	Arabic and English language music and News Radio Sawa (Arabic: راديو سوا‎) is a 24-hour 7-day-a-week Arabic language radio station broadcasting in the Arab world. The station is a service of the Middle East Broadcasting Networks, Inc. and is publicly funded by the Broadcasting Board of Governors and the U.S. Congress.[1] The word "sawa" (سوا, IPA: [ˈsæwæ, ˈsawa]) means "together" in many spoken Arabic dialects.  Preexisting attitudes and concurrent reality of opinions towards the United States led to the creation of Radio Sawa. It seeks to effectively communicate with the youthful population of Arabic-speakers in the Middle East. The station's goal is to promote pro-American attitudes to youth in the Arab world. Radio Sawa's first broadcast was on March 23, 2002. Its newscasts are broadcast live on air from its studios in Washington, DC and Dubai, United Arab Emirates. Radio Sawa also has news bureaus and reporters throughout the Middle East	Public Radio	USA	Arabic	http://mbn-channel-02.akacast.akamaistream.net/7/32/233451/v1/ibb.akacast.akamaistream.net/mbn_channel_02	-	-	-	-	-
